From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] winex11: keep the screen under unerased external shell popups

Purpose: show XP's grey shut down screen instead of a black one. The
dialog's full-screen DimmedWindow has no class background brush, so XP
leaves the screen visible under it; the dialog then reads its own window
back strip by strip and turns it grey. A new Wine surface starts black,
which was read back and kept. Extend the 0042 underlay, which copies the
root pixels into a new non-layered popup's buffer, to popups whose class
has no background brush. Limited to the opted-in external shell.

diff --git a/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c b/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
index 318958e..022776c 100644
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
@@ -2886,7 +2886,10 @@ BOOL X11DRV_WindowPosChanging( HWND hwnd, UINT swp_flags, BOOL shaped, const str
         (NtUserGetWindowLongW( hwnd, GWL_EXSTYLE ) & WS_EX_LAYERED))
         data->preserve_no_redraw = FALSE;
     else if (swp_flags & SWP_SHOWWINDOW)
-        data->preserve_no_redraw = getenv( "WIN4WINE_EXTERNAL_SHELL" ) && (swp_flags & SWP_NOREDRAW);
+        /* A popup whose class has no background brush never erases what lies
+         * under it either; XP's shut down screen reads that back to dim it. */
+        data->preserve_no_redraw = getenv( "WIN4WINE_EXTERNAL_SHELL" ) &&
+            ((swp_flags & SWP_NOREDRAW) || !NtUserGetClassLongPtrW( hwnd, GCLP_HBRBACKGROUND ));
 
     /* check if we need to switch the window to managed */
     if (!data->managed && data->whole_window && is_window_managed( hwnd, swp_flags, &rects->window ))
